# Default deny. Everything is ignored unless it is inside a directory, or is a
# file, named in the allow list below. Adding a source file to an allowed
# directory needs no edit here; adding a new directory does.
*
!*/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Allow list: the directories and files that make up the repository.
# Only what is executable or checkable is tracked: the kernel and the
# components, the gates and their inputs, the proofs, the evidence, the paper,
# the charter. Notes live outside the history until the engine is stable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!/.gitattributes
!/Cargo.lock
!/Cargo.toml
!/.gitignore
!/LICENSE-APACHE
!/LICENSE-MIT
!/README.md
!/README.zh.md
!/CHARTER.md
!/CHARTER.zh.md
!/environment.json
!/crates/**
!/engine/**
!/experiments/**
!/paper/**
!/proofs/**
!/scripts/**
!/.dsh/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ignored even inside an allowed directory: build products, machine-local
# configuration, untracked inputs, and files removed from tracking on purpose.
# A later match wins, so these override the allow list above.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.library/
.local/
.repo/
.metaform/
dist/
tmp/
engine/target/
/target/
crates/*/target/
research/
proofs/.lake/
experiments/lean_oracle/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pdf
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.png
engine/last-test.log
crates/*/last-test.log
proofs/last-check.log
scripts/local.ps1

# Served the local corpus, which is not tracked.
scripts/download-library.ps1
scripts/extract-archives.ps1
scripts/extract-pdf-text.ps1
scripts/verify-library.ps1
scripts/library-manifest.json

# Lake scaffolding for the borrowed project: regenerated, never tracked.
proofs/lakefile.toml
proofs/lake-manifest.json
proofs/lean-toolchain

# Run output of the experiments: state files, responses, working directories.
experiments/tmp/
crates/*/Cargo.lock

# Metered-run metrics. tmp/ already ignores this; the explicit rule keeps the
# output path intentional if the broad tmp rule is ever narrowed.
tmp/metrics/

# Conversation dumps and internal notes.
1.md
1-digest.md
2.md
3.md
reasoning_engine_research_map.md
HANDOFF.md
